In article <23390@ucdavis.ucdavis.edu> zerkle@cs.ucdavis.edu (Dan Zerkle) writes:
>I suppose these could be spoilers:

>
>There are a bunch of monster-specific artifact weapons in NH.  Off the
>top of my head, they are:
>
>Sunsword	(undead)
>Demonbane
>Ogresmasher
>Orcrist
>Dragonbane
>Sting		(orcs)
>Giantslayer
>Trollsbane
>Werebane
>
>These weapons are +5 to hit and double damage against the
>specific creatures.  They are all lawful, except for Dragonbane and
>Giantslayer (neutral).
>
>With the exception of Werebane (it's silver), none of these is any
>better than a general purpose artifact (such as Frost Brand or
>Mjollnir) in fighting the appropriate monster.  You get no special
>attack messages, and no effects other than double damage (which you
>can get with Frost Brand or Fire Brand anyway).
>
>In fact these weapons are generally so useless that I toss them aside
>as soon as I find them.
>
>Therefore, I propose that these weapons be made more useful.  Here are
>a couple ideas:
>
>Make the weapons a little better against non-specific monsters.  They
>could simply add an extra +1 to damage and hit.  This makes sense
>because these artifacts are specially crafted and extra high quality.
>While the magic would only work against the right creatures, the extra
>quality of manufacture would work on all opponents.
>
>Give extra effects when attacking specific monsters.  The Magicbane
>effects (minus purging and probing, perhaps) would be perfect.
>Monsters would have legends about that hideous sword (or morning star,
>or dagger, or whatever).  Upon recognizing it or being hit with it,
>they would be prone to running away or being stunned with terror.
>
>Make Dragonbane a lance, fer cryin' out loud.
>
>Give special messages:  
>"You smash the ogre!"
>"The rock troll roars in agony!"
>"The hill orc screams with terror!"
>"You pierce the blue dragon deeply!"
>
>The messages wouldn't make the weapon more effective, but they would
>make it more fun!
>
>--
>Dan Zerkle  zerkle@cs.ucdavis.edu  (916) 756-5170

I like these ideas, but I'd go even further.  I think they should be the best
weapon against those monsters, but just a normal weapon against all others.
So say.....  triple damage vs those monsters, with a good chance of instant
death (a better chance than Vorpal Blade has) (You smash in the ogre's skull!
The demon screams and disappears as your blade hits it!) But against
all other monsters, just a normal weapon (or whatever it's enchantment is)..






